      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The selective application of sanctions is a fundamental and undeniable flaw in the current international system. When powerful nations selectively target adversaries while overlooking the transgressions of their allies, it reveals that these tools are not objective instruments of justice. Instead, they function as instruments of foreign policy leverage, reinforcing the existing hierarchy of global power. This hypocrisy undermines any claim that sanctions are a purely principled means of promoting democracy.",
